# Bill of materials rules content


Admin BoM Workflow Structure!!!! 

1. Login and Dashboard Access 

Admin logs in and lands on the Admin Dashboard. 

Dashboard displays:  

Overview of all projects 

Notifications (low stock, pending requests, transfers, returns) 

Quick links to BoM management, reports, and user management 

Shape 

2. Project and BoM Management 

Admin selects a project to view or manage its BoM. 

System displays:  

Full BoM for the project (materials, categories, quantities, usage, remaining, low-stock indicators) 

Options to adjust allocations, correct errors, or set thresholds 

Shape 

3. Material Request Handling 

Admin reviews new material requests (from project managers/users). 

For each request:  

View material, quantity, reason, and attachments 

Decide: Approve, Deny, or Adjust Quantity 

(Optional) Add comment for decision 

System updates:  

If approved: Updates project BoM, notifies requester 

If denied: Notifies requester with reason 

All actions logged in audit trail 

Shape 

4. Material Transfer Handling 

Admin reviews transfer requests (move material between projects). 

For each transfer:  

View source/destination projects, material, quantity, reason 

Decide: Approve or Deny 

(Optional) Add comment 

System updates:  

If approved: Updates BoMs for both projects, notifies involved users 

If denied: Notifies requester 

All actions logged 

Shape 

5. Material Return Handling 

Admin reviews return requests (unused/damaged material). 

For each return:  

View material, quantity, reason, attachments 

Decide: Approve or Deny 

(Optional) Add comment 

System updates:  

If approved: Updates project BoM, notifies requester 

If denied: Notifies requester 

All actions logged 

Shape 

6. Material Catalog Management 

Admin manages master material list:  

Add new materials (name, category, unit, cost, supplier) 

Edit or deactivate materials 

Categorize materials for easy searching 

Shape 

7. Reporting and Analysis 

Admin generates reports:  

BoM per project or company-wide 

Material usage, costs, trends 

Export options (PDF, Excel) 

Admin reviews audit trail:  

All user/system actions for traceability 

Shape 

8. User and Permission Management 

Admin manages users:  

Assign project managers 

Set or revoke permissions 

Define user roles 

Shape 

9. Notifications and Alerts 

Admin receives notifications:  

Low stock 

New/pending requests 

Approvals/denials 

System alerts 

Shape 

10. Logout or Switch Project 

Admin can log out or switch to another project to repeat the workflow. 

